FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-land-surveyor.
OFF THE RECORD: a filesystem, in the only sense that matters here: an
OFF THE RECORD: append-only archive of immutable documents, and a
OFF THE RECORD: compacted catalog pointing each name at its current
OFF THE RECORD: version. Saving appends and repoints; nothing is ever
OFF THE RECORD: overwritten, so version history is the archive itself.

ARTICLE 1.
    COMMIT "I request admission to the Castle." TO THE ARCHIVE AS "petition".
    COMMIT "I request admission to the village." TO THE ARCHIVE AS "petition".
    COMMIT "I request a post as school janitor." TO THE ARCHIVE AS "petition".
    PROCLAIM THE DOCUMENT "petition" FROM THE ARCHIVE.
    PROCLAIM "The earlier drafts are retained, and will be considered.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
